If anyone out there has a profiled run of a Nethack v3.0 patch level 9
game with the wizard character, would you please send me a copy of the
profile or simply tell me which object modules are called the most
frequently?  I need to know which object modules are called the most
frequently so that I can get the game to work with the overlay manager
of Turbo C++ v3.0 with the fewest disk accesses.  The default NEARDATA
configuration seems sub-optimal for use with Turbo C++ v3.0.  I have
been able to get a significant speed-up by guessing which object modules
are called the most frequently and using a disk cache, but I
wonder if there is a better way.


